    "abstract": "Aretaeus of Cappadocia is a controversial figure in the history of ancient Greek medicine. No one denied that he was a physician who formed the most accurate descriptions of diseases in antiquity. Such an example is his to the point analysis about phthisis, which, according to modern medicine, can be identified as pulmonary tuberculosis in Chapter VIII of his First Book on Chronic Diseases.",
