    "localPdfUrl": "js/data/pdfs/295.pdf",
    "previewText": "Abstract Background: Penetrating neck injuries result from missiles and stab wounds. A gas pistol is a non-lethal weapon for self-defence. Case Report: We present a case where the use of a modified gun led to multiple injuries in a single shot. Four projectiles were embedded in the neck, one in the larynx and three in the cervical spine. The first was removed via a combined external and endoscopic approach, while the rest were put on follow-up. Conclusion: The reported case shows that damage from modified gas pistols, although rarely life threatening, may cause long term discomfort and diminished quality of life.",
    "abstractHtml": "<div class=\"col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12\">\n\t\t\t<h3>\r\n\tAbstract</h3>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Background</strong>: Penetrating neck injuries result from missiles and stab wounds. A gas pistol is a non-lethal weapon for self-defence.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Case Report</strong>: We present a case where the use of a modified gun led to multiple injuries in a single shot. Four projectiles were embedded in the neck, one in the larynx and three in the cervical spine. The first was removed via a combined external and endoscopic approach, while the rest were put on follow-up.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Conclusion</strong>: The reported case shows that damage from modified gas pistols, although rarely life threatening, may cause long term discomfort and diminished quality of life.</p>\r\n \t\t\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>",
