    "abstractHtml": "<div class=\"col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12\">\n\t\t\t<h3>\r\n\tAbstract</h3>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Objectives</strong>: End-stage renal disease is a worldwide public health problem. While the survival time of the patients extends, additional pathologies such as secondary hyperparathyroidism occurs. The aim of the study is to review the surgical approaches to secondary hyperparathyroidism and present our experiences.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Patients and Methods</strong>: This retrospective study included five male patients (mean age 38.6 years) who were operated on for chronic renal failure between 2004 and 2008. The data of patients were collected from hospital records.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Results</strong>: The mean duration of hemodialysis was 106.8 months. All patients had ultrasonography and scintigraphy preoperatively. The mean value of preoperative and postoperative serum PTH was 2097 ng/ml and 36.5 ng/dl, Ca 11.48 mg/dl and 6.2 mg/dl, P 7.5 mg/dl and 4.4 mg/dl, ALP 527 IU/L and 89 IU/L. Total parathyroidectomy and sternocleidomastoid muscle autotransplantation was performed in all patients and one patient had right thyroidectomy in addition. Postoperatively, all patients received oral calcium carbonate and calcitriol. No serious postoperative complications occurred in any of these cases. The duration of hospitalization was 4.6 days on the average. Serum PTH was kept constantly below 300 ng/L in all cases in follow-up and no recurrent hyperparathyroidism was detected.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Conclusion</strong>: Although there are many types of surgery techniques in treatment of secondary hyperparathyroidism, total parathyroidectomy with autografting is the most accepted procedure with low recurrent and complication rate in end-stage renal disease patients.</p>\r\n<h3>\r\n\tTurkish</h3>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Ama&ccedil;</strong>: Son d&ouml;nem b&ouml;brek hastalığı d&uuml;nya &ccedil;apında bir sağlık problemidir. Bu hastaların yaşam s&uuml;releri uzadık&ccedil;a sekonder hiperparatiroidizm gibi ek patolojiler de gelişmektedir. Bu &ccedil;alışmanın amacı sekonder hiperparatiroidizme cerrahi yaklaşımları g&ouml;zden ge&ccedil;irmek ve kendi tecr&uuml;belerimizi sunmaktır.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Hastalar ve Y&ouml;ntemler</strong>: Bu retrospektif &ccedil;alışmaya 2004 ve 2008 yılları arasında kronik b&ouml;brek hastalığı tanısıyla ameliyat edilen beş erkek hasta (ort. yaş 38.6) dahil edildi. Hasta bilgileri hastane kayıtlarından toplandı.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Bulgular</strong>: Hastaların ortalama hemodiyaliz s&uuml;resi 106.8 aydı. B&uuml;t&uuml;n hastalar ameliyat &ouml;ncesi d&ouml;nemde ultrasonografi ve sintigrafi ile incelendi. Hastaların ameliyat &ouml;ncesi ve sonrası d&ouml;nemde ortalama serum PTH değeri 2097 ng/ ml ve 36.5 ng/dl, Ca 11.48 mg/dl ve 6.2 mg/dl, P 7.5 mg/dl ve 4.4 mg/dl, ALP 527 IU/L ve 89 IU/L idi. B&uuml;t&uuml;n hastalara total paratiroidektomi ve sternokleidomastoid kasa ototransplantasyon yapılırken bir hastaya ek olarak sağ tiroidektomi yapıldı. Ameliyat sonrası d&ouml;nemde t&uuml;m hastalar oral kalsiyum karbonat ve kalsitriol kullandılar. Hi&ccedil;bir hastada ciddi komplikasyon g&ouml;r&uuml;lmedi. Ortalama hastanede kalış s&uuml;resi 4.6 g&uuml;nd&uuml;. Hastaların hepsinde serum PTH d&uuml;zeyleri 300 ng/dl altında seyretti ve hi&ccedil;bir hastada takipler esnasında n&uuml;ks hiperparatiroidizm g&ouml;r&uuml;lmedi.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\t<strong>Sonu&ccedil;</strong>: Sekonder hiperparatiroidizmin cerrahi tedavisi i&ccedil;in bir&ccedil;ok y&ouml;ntem olsa da total paratiroidektomi ve ototransplantasyon d&uuml;ş&uuml;k n&uuml;ks ve komplikasyon oranları ile son d&ouml;nem b&ouml;brek hastalarında gelişen sekonder hiperparatiroidizmin i&ccedil;in en kabul edilen tedavi metotlarındandır.</p>\r\n \t\t\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>",
